    "text": "human beings"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:16.560",
    "end": "00:01:19.969",
    "text": "they are therefore called aparshayas"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:19.979",
    "end": "00:01:23.030",
    "text": "for centuries The Vedas have been handed"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:23.040",
    "end": "00:01:26.450",
    "text": "over to the posterity by World tradition"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:26.460",
    "end": "00:01:29.990",
    "text": "the great Saint SRI krishnaipayana who"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:30.000",
    "end": "00:01:33.109",
    "text": "is also called vyasa acharya arranged"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:33.119",
    "end": "00:01:36.050",
    "text": "these Vedas into four categories which"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:36.060",
    "end": "00:01:41.510",
    "text": "are called"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:41.520",
    "end": "00:01:44.030",
    "text": "each of these Vedas consists of three"
  },
  {
    "start": "00:01:44.040",
